  "interpretation": [
    "All three arms use the same new source, fixed model, single thread and Legacy mode; these are not old-version versus new-version measurements.",
    "Baseline uses greedy search; both supplied-note arms use modified beam search. Positive-versus-negative is the available same-decoder comparison.",
    "Raw complete-name recall is 30/100 baseline, 44/100 positive, 30/100 negative. Corrected recall is 30,47,30; 53 positive names remain missed.",
    "The designated unspoken negative name appeared in 0/100 negative arms; this does not prove absence of other invented text or all possible false positives.",
    "English public read speech and imported WAVs do not establish Chinese, code-switching, natural meetings, live microphone, speaker attribution, captions, minutes, other hardware or install/upgrade acceptance.",
    "Sampled RSS/CPU and decoder RTF are bounded observations with uncontrolled OS page caches, not whole-application resource reductions or real-time performance.",
    "Previous six-arm smoke FAIL report remains unchanged; its prepared-PCM comparison was invalid for production PcmReader preprocessing. The independent offline review confirms all six archived PCM/WAV payloads match the canonical decoder while separately retaining missing-hotword and real recognition failures.",
    "The original manual mixed-language minutes case Q16 still fails; 0.3.5 has not been released.",
    "The negative hint arm trades one recalled name for one missed name relative to baseline; its unchanged total must not be called absence of regressions. A zero negative-name count is not zero population risk and its all-zero bootstrap interval is degenerate."
  ],
